    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Practice -ir",
        "body": "Vivir is an infinitive in the Spanish -ir family. Its stem is viv-, and its present endings for yo, tú, and él are -o, -es, and -e.\n\nViv- plus -o makes yo vivo; plus -es makes tú vives; plus -e makes él vive. Escribir follows the same route: escribo, escribes, escribe.\n\nPractice: Conjugate abrir and vivir for yo, tú, and él. Mark each stem and circle each ending.\n\nCommon mistake: Do not call a verb -er just because tú ends in -es. Check the infinitive first."
      }
    ],
